OL,3,GNEWSA'Summer was a wake-up call, winter
OL,4,Acould be dire' warning over food
OL,5,Asupplies
OL,6,
OL,7,FDroughts and wildfires in the summer
OL,8,Fwere a wake-up call, and winter
OL,9,Fflooding could leave Wales' food supply
OL,10,Fvulnerable, an expert has warned.
OL,12,FThe country currently imports the vast
OL,13,Fmajority of its fruit and vegetables,
OL,14,Fwith only 6% of those served in its
OL,15,Fschools grown in Wales.
OL,17,FIt is dependent on produce from parts
OL,18,Fof the world prone to droughts and
OL,19,Ffires, according to co-founder of an
OL,20,Forganisation aiming to address this.
OL,23,APub: 11-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,437,430,260,140,0,100
